From: local <local@local>
Date: Mon, 10 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: aspeed: tiogapass: disable KCS2 at 0xCA8

TiogaPass only uses KCS3 (0xCA2) for host IPMI.  KCS2 was enabled in
the upstream DTS at 0xCA8 but there is no BMC userspace handler for it
(kcsbridged only runs for KCS3).

When FM_BMC_READY_N is properly asserted, the host BIOS fully initialises
and populates the SMBIOS IPMI entry pointing at 0xCA8.  The host kernel's
ipmi_si driver probes 0xCA8, finds ASPEED KCS2 hardware responding
(HICR0 LPC2E bit set = ACKs LPC cycles), sends "Get Device ID", and
waits for OBF which is never set because no BMC code reads the incoming
message.  ipmi_si registers this dead interface as /dev/ipmi0.  Any
ipmitool call on the host uses /dev/ipmi0 and hangs indefinitely,
preventing the host OS from completing boot.

Disable KCS2 so the ASPEED hardware ignores LPC cycles at 0xCA8.
ipmi_si reads 0xFF, determines no hardware is present, and falls through
to KCS3 at 0xCA2 which has a working BMC userspace handler.

Signed-off-by: local <local@local>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-facebook-tiogapass.dts | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-facebook-tiogapass.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-facebook-tiogapass.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-facebook-tiogapass.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-facebook-tiogapass.dts
@@ -125,9 +125,8 @@
 };

 &kcs2 {
-	// BMC KCS channel 2
-	status = "okay";
-	aspeed,lpc-io-reg = <0xca8>;
+	// BMC KCS channel 2 - disabled: no userspace handler, would hang host ipmi_si at 0xCA8
+	status = "disabled";
 };

 &kcs3 {
